 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Agent tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up pages expose their client-side form actions through
+[WebMCP](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/) in supporting browsers:
+
+| Page | Tool | Required inputs |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `/devtools-times/signin` | `sign_in` | `username`, `password` |
+| `/devtools-times/signup` | `sign_up` | `username`, `password` |
+
+Tools register when the form mounts and unregister when it unmounts or Astro
+navigates to another page. Both `document.modelContext` (current draft) and
+`navigator.modelContext` (early preview) are supported. Browsers without WebMCP
+continue to use the forms normally.
+
+Tool calls share the form submission logic and existing authentication APIs,
+update the visible loading/error/success states, and resolve after the request
+finishes. Results contain a text message and `isError`; credentials and API tokens
+are not included. Registration success clears the form, just as manual submission
+does. Sign-in retains the existing behavior and does not persist a token.
+
+Run the isolated tests with `pnpm test` (Node 22.6+); requests and browser APIs are
+mocked, so no server or live account is needed. Run `pnpm build` for build validation.
